{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--shizunai-coastal-inland-variation","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--isogloss-geography"],"statement":{"en":"Dialectal differences exist within Shizunai Ainu between coastal speech and inland speech separated by about twenty kilometers.","ja":"静内アイヌ語の内部において、約20キロメートル離れた海岸部と内陸部の話者の間に方言差が存在する。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"exists","modality":"assertive","conditions":["between coastal and inland speakers"]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:majewicz2022@handbook-epub/l0025-03","stance":"reports"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0058-03","stance":"proposes"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--pa-ca-dialectal-correspondence","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--pa-ca"],"statement":{"en":"Root-initial pa- in southwestern (western) Hokkaido dialects corresponds to ca- in northeastern (eastern) Hokkaido dialects across a set of lexical items.","ja":"一連の語彙において、南西（道西）部方言の語頭 pa- は北東（道東）部方言の ca- に対応する。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest","doculect:hokkaido/northeast"],"quantifier":"exists","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["pa-","ca-","par","car","pas","cas","pan","can"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0108-02","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:nakagawafukazawa2022@handbook-epub/l0050-08","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--in-the-tokachi-dialect-ruwe-tapan-takes-the","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--ay-elision"],"statement":{"en":"In the Tokachi dialect, ruwe tapan takes the form ru tapan.","ja":"十勝方言では ruwe tapan は ru tapan などの形になる。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/central/tokachi"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["ru tapan","ruwe tapan"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0397-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--sittapan-is-sometimes-heard-as-sitapan-with-no","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--ay-elision"],"statement":{"en":"sittapan is sometimes heard as sitapan, with no difference in usage.","ja":"時には sittapan > sitapan のように聞こえる時もあるが、用法としては違いはない。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/central/ishikari"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["sittapan","sitapan"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0398-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--the-form-estap-used-in-sentence-final-phrases","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--ay-elision"],"statement":{"en":"The form estap, used in sentence-final phrases like ru estap an, is found in dialects such as Shiranuka but is especially prominent in the Tokachi dialect.","ja":"estap は白糠方言などにも例は見られるが、特に十勝方言に顕著な形式である。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/central/tokachi"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["estap","ru estap an"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0399-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--in-the-tokachi-dialect-the-secondary-particles-etap","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--ay-elision"],"statement":{"en":"In the Tokachi dialect, the secondary particles etap and tap also appear within sentence-final phrases.","ja":"十勝方言では etap や tap という形もこの文末句の中に出てくることがある。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/central/tokachi"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["etap","tap"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0399-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--the-particle-etap-occurs-in-shiranuka-and-shizunai","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--ay-elision"],"statement":{"en":"The particle etap occurs in Shiranuka and Shizunai dialects, and appears as hetap in other dialects, deriving etymologically from interrogative he plus emphatic tap.","ja":"etap は白糠方言や静内方言にもあり、またそれ以外の方言では hetap という形で出てくる副助詞で、語源的には he（疑問）+ tap（強調）の副助詞であろう。"},"type":"diachrony","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["etap","hetap","he","tap"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0399-04","stance":"proposes"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--using-etap-within-sentence-final-phrases-is-a","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--ay-elision"],"statement":{"en":"Using etap within sentence-final phrases is a usage unique to the Tokachi dialect.","ja":"etap を文末句の中で使うのは、十勝方言独特の用法である。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/central/tokachi"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["etap"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0399-05","stance":"proposes"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--in-dialects-such-as-eastern-hidaka-tokachi-and","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--cluster-assimilation"],"statement":{"en":"In dialects such as Eastern Hidaka, Tokachi, and Eastern Hokkaido (Kushiro, Shiranuka, Bihoro), word-internal stop clusters like -tk-, -pk-, and -kt- show regressive assimilation historically (e.g., hotke → hokke, popke → pokke, rikta → ritta).","ja":"日高東部、十勝、道東（釧路、白糠、美幌）などの方言では、単語内部の -tk-、-pk-、-kt- などの閉鎖音連続が逆行同化を示す（例：hotke → hokke、popke → pokke、rikta → ritta）。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/central/tokachi","doculect:hokkaido/northeast/kushiro","doculect:hokkaido/northeast/kitami"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":["word-internally"]},"forms":["hokke","pokke","ritta","hotke","popke","rikta"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0034-10","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--the-verb-meaning-to-come-is-ek-across","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--consonant-variation"],"statement":{"en":"The verb meaning 'to come' is ek across dialects, corresponding to eh in Sakhalin Ainu.","ja":"「来る」を表す動詞はどの方言でも ek であり、樺太方言では規則的な対応形である eh である。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["ek","eh"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0106-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--in-the-urakawa-and-samani-dialects-an-initial","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--h-elision"],"statement":{"en":"In the Urakawa and Samani dialects, an initial h- is frequently added before words that begin with a vowel in other dialects, as seen in Samani hekimun 'toward the mountains'.","ja":"浦河方言や様似方言では、他方言で母音で始まる語の語頭に h- が加わることが多く見られ、様似方言の hekimun「山へ」などに現れる。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/samani"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["hekimun"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0276-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--in-the-ishikari-tokachi-and-eastern-hokkaido-dialects","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--h-elision"],"statement":{"en":"In the Ishikari, Tokachi, and Eastern Hokkaido dialects, initial h drops from he-/ho- directional adverbs, producing forms starting with e- and o- such as erepasi 'offshore'.","ja":"石狩・十勝・道東方言などでは he-/ho- 方向副詞の語頭の h が脱落し、erepasi「沖へ」のように e- や o- で始まる形になる。"},"type":"alternation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/central/ishikari","doculect:hokkaido/central/tokachi","doculect:hokkaido/northeast"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["erepasi"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0276-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--in-the-tokachi-dialect-the-form-ene-corresponds","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--h-elision"],"statement":{"en":"In the Tokachi dialect, the form ene corresponds to hene.","ja":"十勝方言では ene という語形が hene に対応している。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/central/tokachi"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["ene","hene"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0321-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--the-conjunctions-pokor-and-apkor-are-used-in","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--isogloss-geography"],"statement":{"en":"The conjunctions pokor and apkor are used in Iburi, while pekor and apekor are used in Hidaka, to mean 'as if' ('...ka no gotoku').","ja":"「……かの如く」の意味で、胆振では pokor, apkor を、日高では pekor, apekor を用いる。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/horobetsu","doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["pokor","apkor","pekor","apekor"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0162-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--the-saru-dialect-dictionary-notes-that-kosanu-is","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--isogloss-geography"],"statement":{"en":"The Saru dialect dictionary notes that -kosanu is used upriver from Nibutani, whereas -kosanpa is used by speakers downstream, suggesting a dialectal difference within the Saru dialect.","ja":"沙流方言辞典では -kosanu は二風谷より上で用いられ、川下の話者は -kosanpa を用いるとしており、沙流方言内部の方言差であることが示唆されている。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-kosanu","-kosanpa"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0201-02","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--whereas-the-allative-case-particle-un-is-restricted","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--isogloss-geography"],"statement":{"en":"Whereas the allative case particle un is restricted to western Hokkaido, the adnominal case particle un is distributed in the same form throughout all Hokkaido.","ja":"向格の un が道西部に限られるのに対し、連体格の un は全道に同じ形で分布している。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["un"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0298-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--while-other-case-particles-are-uniform-across-dialects","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--isogloss-geography"],"statement":{"en":"While other case particles are uniform across dialects, allative case particles show significant dialectal variation in Hokkaido, dividing into un (western Hidaka and westward), en (eastern Hidaka to Tokachi), and (e)ne (eastern Hokkaido and Ishikari).","ja":"他の格助詞がどの方言でもほぼ同形であるのに対し、向格助詞は方言差が大きく、日高西部以西の un、日高東部〜十勝の en、道東および石狩の (e)ne の3種に分かれる。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["un","en","(e)ne","ene","ne"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0299-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--there-are-morphological-differences-between-the-ishikari-dialect","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--isogloss-geography"],"statement":{"en":"There are morphological differences between the Ishikari dialect and the dialect(s) of central-south Hokkaidō described by Chiri.","ja":"石狩方言と、知里が記述した北海道中南部方言（群）との間には形態論的な相違が存在する。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/central/ishikari","doculect:hokkaido/southwest"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0036-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--the-saru-piratori-dialect-and-the-shizunai-dialect","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--isogloss-geography"],"statement":{"en":"The Saru (Piratori) dialect and the Shizunai dialect differ considerably despite their close geographical proximity.","ja":"沙流（平取）方言と静内方言は地理的に近接しているにもかかわらず、かなり異なっている。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru","doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0036-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--eastern-and-northern-hokkaido-dialects-obihiro-bihoro-nayoro","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--isogloss-geography"],"statement":{"en":"Eastern and northern Hokkaido dialects, Obihiro, Bihoro, Nayoro, Sōya, and Sakhalin have tek or tekka meaning 'after (doing A, to do B)'.","ja":"北海道東部・北部方言、帯広、美幌、名寄、宗谷、および樺太には、「（Aをして）から（Bをする）」という意味のtekまたはtekkaがみられる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/central/tokachi","doculect:hokkaido/northeast/kitami","doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["tek","tekka"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0240-09","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--having-uy-where-other-dialects-have-iw-is","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--metathesis"],"statement":{"en":"Having -uy where other dialects have -iw is a characteristic sound alternation (metathesis) found especially in Bihoro and Kushiro.","ja":"他方言で -iw のところに -uy を持つ交替（音位転換の一種）は、特に美幌方言および釧路方言の特徴である。"},"type":"alternation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/northeast/kitami","doculect:hokkaido/northeast/kushiro"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-iw","-uy","síwnin","suynin","cíw","cuy"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawafukazawa2022@handbook-epub/l0050-10","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--in-dialects-other-than-saru-and-chitose-the","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--other-consonant"],"statement":{"en":"In dialects other than Saru and Chitose, the form erampetek is used instead of erampewtek.","ja":"沙流・千歳以外の地域では、erampewtek に当たるものとして erampetek という形が使われる。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":["沙流・千歳以外の地域"]},"forms":["erampetek","erampewtek"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0312-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--in-hattori-and-chiri-1960-tu-appears-as","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--other-consonant"],"statement":{"en":"In Hattori and Chiri (1960), tu appears as cu in the Samani dialect, though this may represent speaker idiolect.","ja":"服部・知里（1960）において様似方言の tu は cu として現れるが、これは話者の個人方言とも考えられる。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/samani"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"possible","conditions":[]},"forms":["tu","cu"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawafukazawa2022@handbook-epub/l0053-05","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--the-transitive-subject-prefix-a-is-reported-only","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--overview"],"statement":{"en":"The transitive subject prefix a- is reported only in a relatively restricted area including Iburi, western Hidaka, Tokachi, Yoichi, and Shakotan, whereas an- is reported across a wide area including the rest of Hokkaido, Sakhalin, and the Kurils.","ja":"他動詞主格接頭辞 a- は胆振、日高西部、十勝、余市、積丹のような比較的限られた地域でしか報告がないのに対し、an- はそれらを除く北海道と樺太、千島を含む極めて広い範囲で報告されている。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido","doculect:sakhalin","doculect:kuril"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["a-","an-"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2004@pdftotext-pieces/l0002-02","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--in-northern-dialects-p-changes-to-ch","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--pa-ca"],"statement":{"en":"In northern dialects, p changes to ch.","ja":"北部方言において p は ch に変化する。"},"type":"alternation","scope":{"doculects":[],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":["in northern dialects"]},"forms":["p","ch"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0028-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--in-southern-dialects-the-change-from-p-to","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--pa-ca"],"statement":{"en":"In southern dialects, the change from p to ch is found only in the single word san-pa > san-cha 'shore'.","ja":"南部方言において p から ch への変化は (san-pa) > san-cha「岸」の1語のみに見られる。"},"type":"frequency","scope":{"doculects":[],"quantifier":"measured","modality":"actual","conditions":["in southern dialects"]},"forms":["san-pa","san-cha"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0028-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--the-set-of-forms-meaning-mouth-includes-par","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--pa-ca"],"statement":{"en":"The set of forms meaning 'mouth' includes par, car, cara, and caru.","ja":"「口」を意味する形式のセットには par、car、cara、caru がある。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["par","car","cara","caru"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawafukazawa2022@handbook-epub/l0049-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--while-the-saru-and-chitose-dialects-clearly-distinguish","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--vowel-alternations"],"statement":{"en":"While the Saru and Chitose dialects clearly distinguish yayrayke 'commit suicide' from yairayke 'thank', some dialects merge both forms into yayrayke without distinction.","ja":"沙流方言や千歳方言では yayrayke「自殺する」と yairayke「感謝する」をはっきりと区別するが、方言によってはどちらも yayrayke となり区別のないところがある。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru","doculect:hokkaido/chitose"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["yayrayke","yairayke"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0040-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--in-the-tokachi-dialect-the-form-monoa-is","revision":1,"topic":"topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topics":["topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation","topic:diachrony/hokkaido-phonological-microvariation--vowel-alternations"],"statement":{"en":"In the Tokachi dialect, the form monoa is contracted to mona and simply means 'to sit'.","ja":"十勝方言では monoa が mona という形に縮約され、意味もただ「座る」ことを指すようになっている。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/central/tokachi"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["monoa","mona"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0489-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
